hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1145","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I heard him from Amr seventy years ago, saying: Amr bin Aws told me, He heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas tell, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The most beloved prayer to God is the prayer of David, who used to sleep.” Midnight, and he stays in prayer for a third of the night, and sleeps a sixth of it. The most beloved of God’s fasts is the fast of David. He used to fast one day and break his fast the next.”"
